.TH WSCREENSAVERS 1 "October 2026" "wscreensavers 1.1.11" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wscreensavers \- Wayland screensaver, live desktop wallpaper, and PAM screen-lock suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wscreensavers
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B wscreensavers ctl
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wscreensavers
runs 25 built-in WebGL2/Canvas visualizers and 300+ external
.BR xscreensaver (1)
and
.B rss-glx
binaries on Wayland compositors (Hyprland, Sway, River, Wayfire, KDE Plasma) using
the
.B zwlr_layer_shell_v1
and
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
Wayland protocols.
.PP
When invoked with no arguments,
.B wscreensavers
opens the desktop Studio Control Center (built with Wails v3 and WebKit2GTK 4.1)
for browsing savers, tuning per-saver parameters, configuring multi-monitor
assignments, and managing the background daemon and live wallpapers.
.PP
External XScreenSaver modules that normally draw onto an X11 root window are
executed inside isolated offscreen
.BR Xvfb (1)
servers and streamed as MJPEG frames onto borderless Wayland
.B OVERLAY
or
.B BACKGROUND
layer-shell surfaces.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-saver
Launch the fullscreen Wayland screensaver overlay across all connected monitors.
Moving the mouse or pressing any key dismisses the overlay.
.TP
.B \-\-lock
Launch the fullscreen locked Wayland screensaver overlay across all monitors.
Requires PAM password authentication (or delegates to
.BR hyprlock (1)
/
.BR swaylock (1)
when configured) before unmapping.
.TP
.B \-\-wallpaper
Launch the live wallpaper renderer on the Wayland
.B BACKGROUND
layer-shell surface with an empty input region so pointer clicks pass through to
the desktop and windows above it.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Run the headless idle-detection, saver-cycling, and local HTTP control daemon.
Monitors Wayland seat activity via
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
(with a fallback to
.B hyprctl cursorpos
on Hyprland), inhibits activation during active PipeWire/ALSA audio playback or
fullscreen windows, and manages DPMS monitor power-off timers.
.TP
.B \-\-web
Run the Studio Control Center as a local HTTP web server on
.I 127.0.0.1:8642
without opening a native desktop window.
.TP
.BI \-\-saver\-id " ID"
Override the configured screensaver and run the specified saver ID (for example,
.B matrix3d
or
.BR xss_glmatrix ).
Use
.B per-monitor
with
.B \-\-wallpaper
to assign distinct savers per display output.
.TP
.BI \-\-server\-url " URL"
Connect overlay or wallpaper views to an existing local
.B wscreensavers
HTTP asset/stream server instead of starting an embedded listener.
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " HOST:PORT"
Set the HTTP listen address for
.B \-\-daemon
and
.B \-\-web
modes (default:
.IR 127.0.0.1:8642 ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the
.B wscreensavers
version and exit.
.SH CTL SUBCOMMANDS
The
.B wscreensavers ctl
interface controls the running daemon or spawns detached overlay/wallpaper
processes from shell scripts, window-manager keybindings, or the Noctalia Shell
plugin. Most subcommands print the updated status payload as JSON.
.TP
.B status\fR, \fBget
Print the current configuration, active saver names, live wallpaper state,
detected monitor outputs, and available saver catalog as JSON.
.TP
.BI "launch " "[SAVER_ID]"
Start the fullscreen screensaver immediately. If
.I SAVER_ID
is omitted, uses the configured saver or picks the next entry from the shuffle
pool when mode is
.B random
or
.BR cycle .
.TP
.BI "lock " "[SAVER_ID]"
Lock all monitors immediately using the configured lock provider and saver.
.TP
.B stop\fR, \fBunlock
Dismiss any running screensaver or lock overlay and restore the live wallpaper
if enabled.
.TP
.BR "randomize " "[launch]"
Select the next saver from the non-repeating shuffle pool and update
.IR selectedSaver .
Pass
.B launch
to immediately start the newly selected saver.
.TP
.B wallpaper \fR[\fBtoggle\fR|\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBshuffle\fR] [\fISAVER_ID\fR]
Control the Wayland layer-shell live wallpaper.
.B shuffle
assigns a random native WebGL visualizer to each connected monitor in
.B per-monitor
mode.
.TP
.BI "set " "KEY VALUE"
Update a configuration key in
.I ~/.config/wscreensavers/config.json
and apply changes to running wallpaper or daemon processes. See
.B CONFIGURATION KEYS
below.
.TP
.B pool toggle \fISAVER_ID\fR | \fBpool all\fR | \fBpool none
Add or remove a saver from the random/cycle shuffle pool, enable all discovered
savers, or clear the pool.
.TP
.B gui
Launch the Studio Control Center desktop window in the background.
.TP
.B nag \fR[\fBoff\fR|\fBdisable\fR|\fBstatus\fR]
Permanently disable or inspect the startup community support reminder.
.TP
.B version
Print the
.B wscreensavers
version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION KEYS
Keys accepted by
.BR "wscreensavers ctl set " "\fIKEY VALUE\fR:"
.TP
.B mode
Screensaver selection mode:
.BR single ,
.BR random ,
or
.BR cycle .
.TP
.B selectedSaver\fR, \fBsaver
Default screensaver ID (for example,
.BR bughouse3d ,
.BR matrix3d ,
.BR flurry ,
.BR xss_endgame ).
.TP
.B multiMonitorMode
Multi-monitor behavior for screensavers:
.B clone
(same saver on all outputs) or
.B independent
(separate random saver per monitor).
.TP
.B idleTimeoutMinutes
Minutes of seat inactivity before the screensaver activates (positive integer).
.TP
.B cycleTimeoutMinutes
Minutes before rotating to the next saver in
.B cycle
mode (positive integer).
.TP
.B lockEnabled
Whether idle activation locks the screen (\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR).
.TP
.B lockProvider
Lock implementation:
.B internal
(built-in PAM overlay),
.BR hyprlock ,
or
.BR swaylock .
.TP
.B showClockOnSaver
Display a digital clock HUD overlay on active screensavers (\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR).
.TP
.B inhibitOnAudio
Suppress idle activation while PipeWire, PulseAudio, or ALSA audio streams are
playing (\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR).
.TP
.B inhibitOnFullscreen
Suppress idle activation while a fullscreen application window is focused
(\fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR).
.TP
.B wallpaperSaver
Screensaver ID rendered in single-saver live wallpaper mode, or
.BR random .
.TP
.B wallpaperMode
Live wallpaper layout:
.B single
or
.BR per-monitor .
.TP
.B wallpaperPerMonitor
Assign a saver to a specific monitor output in the form
.IB MONITOR = SAVER_ID
(for example,
.BR DP-1=bughouse3d ).
.TP
.B wallpaperFpsCap
Frame rate cap for live wallpapers (integer >= 5, default 30).
.TP
.B xssMaxStreamDim
Maximum long-edge resolution in pixels for offscreen Xvfb XScreenSaver streams
(320\(en3840, default 1920).
.TP
.B dpmsOffMinutes
Minutes after screensaver activation before powering off displays via DPMS
(0 disables DPMS power-off).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland compositor socket used by GTK3 and
.BR gtk-layer-shell .
.TP
.B WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER
Set to
.B 1
by default at startup to prevent WebKit2GTK DMA-BUF protocol crashes on
NVIDIA and wlroots/Hyprland setups.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for user configuration (defaults to
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory used for per-mode singleton flock files
(\fIwscreensavers-daemon.lock\fR, \fIwscreensavers-saver.lock\fR,
\fIwscreensavers-lock.lock\fR, \fIwscreensavers-wallpaper.lock\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wscreensavers/config.json
User configuration file storing saver selections, per-saver parameter overrides,
timeouts, and multi-monitor mappings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/wscreensavers/shuffle.json
Persisted deck state for non-repeating random saver selection.
.TP
.I /usr/share/xscreensaver/config/*.xml
System XScreenSaver XML module definitions parsed automatically at startup.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/xscreensaver/*\fR, \fI/usr/libexec/xscreensaver/*
External XScreenSaver binaries executed inside offscreen Xvfb sessions.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/wscreensavers.service
Systemd user unit for running
.B wscreensavers \-\-daemon
automatically on graphical session login.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open the Studio Control Center GUI:
.PP
.nf
.RS
wscreensavers
.RE
.fi
.PP
Enable and start the background idle daemon via systemd:
.PP
.nf
.RS
systemctl --user enable --now wscreensavers.service
.RE
.fi
.PP
Bind a lock keybinding in
.I ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf
(Hyprland):
.PP
.nf
.RS
bind = $mainMod, L, exec, wscreensavers ctl lock
.RE
.fi
.PP
Start a live wallpaper with a specific 3D scene across all monitors:
.PP
.nf
.RS
wscreensavers ctl wallpaper on bughouse3d
.RE
.fi
.PP
Assign different live wallpapers to two monitors:
.PP
.nf
.RS
wscreensavers ctl set wallpaperPerMonitor DP-1=matrix3d
wscreensavers ctl set wallpaperPerMonitor HDMI-A-1=starwars
wscreensavers ctl wallpaper on
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, configuration error, or failed IPC command.
